  "assumptions": [
    "Q: one unchanged prepared packet of per-row INT8 and FP32 scales for QB and index-Q on eight source layers. Other layers have one Q quantization or no local Q. Removing a norm write additionally requires no BF16 value user; retain the rounded value within the kernel and preserve quantization arithmetic. Layer Q and post-RoPE index quantizations are distinct. The two Q projections retain separate outputs/pitches.",
    "FFN: router consumes FP32 widened after BF16 rounding; shared expert consumes rounded BF16 through DynamicQuant. Norm triple-output fusion retains required BF16/FP32 outputs and produces exactly the shared INT8 codes/scales. Estimate extra pre-router time as old DQ duration less one BF16 read priced at dense copy rate. Existing same-stream shared DQ is erased at its original location. Clock intervals apply to the last F21 entry and shared-add reader; assume translation of F21 service and fixed remaining schedule.",
    "Routed-to-shared alternative adds a contiguous shared packet in original local row order. Do not alias six permuted dispatch copies with padded stride to dense GEMM input. Entire local shared DQ is kept if valid sender count differs from shared M. Count equality still requires matching row IDs, per-row scale, zero and nonfinite conventions, rounding, and a unique writer. The charged store uses dense rate; stalls, recomputation of missing rows, and any separate rounding or code generation for the shared packet can consume additional time.",
    "F21 preparation and shared-fusion estimates overlap. If shared quant is already hidden behind routing in a new concurrent schedule, no separate 40-site graph credit can be added. The unchanged flag-only overlap path was excluded under the fixed fused-MC2 configuration. Independent percentile changes do not add. All estimates refer to a finite batch and are not general hardware ceilings."
  ],
